<title>UK: Reuters' 54th ex-UK air cargo market report.</title>
<headline>Reuters' 54th ex-UK air cargo market report.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Below are the current average ex-UK GBP air cargo market rates per kg for a 100 kg shipment, with a volume-to-weight ratio of six-to-one:</p>
<p>				Oct 30   vs   Oct 16</p>
<p>			  UNITED STATES</p>
<p>LON-JFK		     O.63	    0.62</p>
<p>LON-LAX		     0.73	    0.73</p>
<p>LON-CHI		     0.72	    0.72</p>
<p>			   ASIA-PACIFIC</p>
<p>LON-HKG		     1.22	    1.20</p>
<p>LON-SIN		     1.28	    1.26</p>
<p>LON-NRT		     2.06	    2.05</p>
<p>LON-SEL		     1.97	    1.95</p>
<p>LON-SYD		     2.12	    2.10</p>
<p>			   MIDDLE EAST</p>
<p>LON-DXB		     0.85	    0.80</p>
<p>LON-BAH		     0.98	    0.95</p>
<p>			   AFRICA</p>
<p>LON-JNB		     1.80	    1.65</p>
<p>			   SCANDINAVIA</p>
<p>LON-STO		     0.72		0.71</p>
<p>LON-CPH		     0.65		0.65</p>
<p>			    LATIN AMERICA</p>
<p>LON-SAO		     2.06		2.06</p>
<p>*The rates quoted in this report were obtained by Reuters journalists on confidential basis from a range of airlines, large forwarders and smaller air cargo agents based at the three main London airports.</p>
<p>*All prices quoted in sterling.</p>
<p>*The tariffs represent average rates calculated from a range of prices and are indicative or current market activity. -- Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax +44 171 542 5017</p>
